# What travels between src/ and hermes:/home/www/rpg — read by BOTH deploy.sh
# and pull.sh with `--exclude-from`, so the two cannot drift apart.
#
# One list for both directions is the point, not a convenience. pull.sh runs
# rsync with --delete, and rsync never deletes an EXCLUDED path on the
# receiving side (short of --delete-excluded, which nothing here passes). So a
# path deploy.sh does not push must also be one pull.sh does not see, or the
# first pull after it vanishes from hermes deletes the local copy — src/sql,
# src/docs and src/tools would go exactly that way.
#
# hermes serves /home/www/rpg as its web root under nginx, which reads no
# .htaccess: anything that lands there is downloadable by URL. Hence the rule
# for adding a line: if the running site neither serves it nor reads it, it
# does not go. Every entry below was checked against the PHP and JS for a
# runtime read (file_get_contents/is_file/glob/include) before it was added.
# The nginx rules in docker/nginx/deny-private.conf are the second fence, for
# whatever is already up there and for whatever slips past this list.
#
# Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth; with one, only at the
# top of src/.

# Local dev credentials must never overwrite prod's, and prod's must never come
# down. CLAUDE.md, "Things that will bite you".
/app/config/database.php

# Schema, seed, generated content.sql and the migrations. content.sql is every
# quest and every line of dialogue in the game; schema.sql is the database's
# shape. Migrations are applied on hermes by hand, never by a deploy. Nothing
# reads these at runtime — the two mentions in app/lib are error messages
# naming a migration to run.
/sql/
*.sql

# Operational tools. NONE of the PHP files in there guards on php_sapi_name(),
# so deploying them would put repair_save.php, end_open_delves.php, the
# backfill_* scripts and forty test harnesses on the public site, ready to run
# against the live database — test_delve.php alone opens with
# `DELETE FROM regions`. Every reference to `tools/` in the app is a comment,
# and the one file it generates (assets/css/dice.css) ships as an asset. If an
# operational tool is ever wanted on hermes, the fix is a CLI guard on that
# tool, not this line removed.
/tools/
/tests/

# Design notes, READMEs and art prompt sheets (docs/*.md, content/README.md,
# assets/**/README.md, assets/images/locations/PROMPTS_*.md, embed/README.md).
# Spoilers at best. Nothing renders markdown from disk.
/docs/
*.md

# Scratch output from verification runs, checked in at the top of src/. NOT
# `*.txt`: assets/fonts/**/OFL.txt are the fonts' licences and have to travel
# with them.
/verify*.txt

# Scripts, build litter and editor droppings.
*.py
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.sh
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.swp

# Dotfiles and dot-directories: .git, .gitignore (embed/ has one),
# .claude/settings.local.json (per-machine), .DS_Store. Nothing in the site is
# a dotfile. hermes's /.well-known/ (certbot) is not under src/ and, being
# excluded here, is never touched by a deploy nor deleted by a pull.
.*

# One line read by each of the speech model's non-English voices, generated by
# `gen_voiceover.py --sample-accents` so a human can decide by ear whether any
# of them belong in the cast. Referenced by no page and no manifest; the clips
# the game plays are named for a hash of their words in assets/audio/vo/<npc>/.
_accent_samples/

# The character look library (assets/looks/, ~0.6 GB, ~51k WebP files baked
# by tools/bake_looks.py). It IS served — the game draws every player's
# portrait and board figure out of it — but it is not deploy.sh's to send:
# a 51k-file tree would turn every routine deploy into a long rsync scan, and
# it changes on a different clock from the code (when the creator snapshot is
# re-baked, not when PHP changes). It travels by its own script (not written
# yet — PR6). Excluded here so deploy.sh never pushes it, and — the reason
# the list is shared — so pull.sh's --delete never deletes a local bake that
# hermes does not have yet.
/assets/looks/
